    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Multiplying by \\(\\sqrt{x}\\) gives \\[ 2x+2=5\\sqrt{x}. \\] Squaring and simplifying, \\[ 4x^2+8x+4=25x, \\] so \\[ 4x^2-17x+4=0. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply by \\(\\sqrt{x}\\) to remove the negative exponent",
        "Isolate the radical in \\(2x+2=5\\sqrt{x}\\) before squaring"
      ],
